For my Requirements Engineering project I have chosen scenario A - Community Volunteer & Event Coordination System.

A community organisation runs local events and activities throughout the year.
Volunteers currently sign up using email, phone calls, spreadsheets and paper forms.
The organisation is considering a software system to help coordinate volunteers and
events.

Current problems include:
• organisers spend a lot of time matching volunteers to activities
• volunteers are sometimes unsure which activities need help
• organisers do not always know who is available
• changes and cancellations can be difficult to communicate
• some activities require particular skills or experience
• organisers need to know who is attending each activity
• volunteer information is currently stored in several places
• accessibility and privacy need to be considered

As the Requirements Engineer, investigate questions such as:
• Who can create or manage an event?
• Who can register as a volunteer?
• What information should volunteers provide?
• How are volunteers matched to activities?
• Are particular skills or qualifications required for some activities?
• How far in advance can someone register?
• What happens when a volunteer cancels?
• What happens if an event changes or is cancelled?
• Can organisers contact all volunteers, selected volunteers, or both?
• What information should different users be able to see?
• Should volunteers be able to see who else is attending?
• What privacy and security requirements might apply?
• What accessibility requirements should be considered? 
